        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nIf I remember correctly the main motivation for this behavior is to be consistent with how cursor is placed *after* operating on textobject. This is [explicitly documented](https://neovim.io/doc/user/motion.html#operator-resulting-pos) while cursor placement after visual selection is more of an implementation detail. At least I am not aware of the explicit documentation on the matter.\r\n\r\nThis was previously closed as not planned (but I can not find right now), but I'll revisit later (and also take a look at whether there are more important implementation reasons for that in 'mini.ai').",
